%% Sanctuary supervisor daemon (MISSION-001 POC): sequence of one job.
%% Source: plugins/sanctuary-core/.apm/skills/running-sanctuary-daemon/scripts/sanctuary_daemon.py (frozen copy: LEARNING/experiments/mission-001/daemon/)
%% The daemon never calls a model. Models run only inside the dispatched job.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Human as Richard (Human Gate)
    participant Agent as Session agent (e.g. Claude Code)
    participant Queue as ~/.sanctuary/daemon/queue/*.json
    participant Daemon as sanctuary_daemon.py (0 tokens)
    participant Runner as cli-agent run_agent.py
    participant Engine as Engine CLI (claude / codex / agy / llama)
    participant Repo as Task worktree (git)

    Note over Human,Daemon: Startup is manual or launchd opt-in. Session bootstrap never starts it.
    Human->>Daemon: sanctuary_daemon.py run
    Daemon->>Queue: recover(): kill and re-queue any job left RUNNING
    loop Idle (kqueue wait, ~0% CPU, no model calls)
        Daemon-->>Queue: wait for directory write event
    end

    Human->>Agent: approve work ("Go")
    Agent->>Queue: enqueue job (authorized_by, runner, timeout_sec) via atomic os.replace
    Queue-->>Daemon: kqueue NOTE_WRITE (detected < 2 s)

    Daemon->>Daemon: gate(job): authorized_by? copilot? bypass flags?
    alt Gate fails
        Daemon->>Queue: status REJECTED + reason (nothing runs)
    else Circuit open (BLOCKED_ON_HUMAN)
        Daemon-->>Queue: leave QUEUED; wait for `reset`
    else Gate passes
        Daemon->>Queue: status RUNNING (pid, pgid, attempts)
        Daemon->>Runner: spawn in new process group (--isolated --cwd --allowed-root --claim-dir --timeout --result-json)
        Runner->>Runner: refuse if cwd escapes allowed root or unit already claimed
        Runner->>Engine: launch headless prompt
        Engine->>Repo: edit, test, commit (inside the worktree)
        alt Finishes in time
            Engine-->>Runner: exit code
            Runner-->>Daemon: exit code + result.json
            Daemon->>Repo: compare HEAD (if require_commit)
            Daemon->>Queue: COMPLETED or FAILED
        else Wall clock > timeout_sec
            Daemon->>Runner: SIGTERM process group, 2 s grace, SIGKILL
            Daemon->>Queue: TIMED_OUT
        end
        alt 3 consecutive failures
            Daemon->>Daemon: daemon_status = BLOCKED_ON_HUMAN
            Daemon-->>Human: status shows circuit open
            Human->>Daemon: sanctuary_daemon.py reset (after review)
        end
    end

    Note over Daemon,Queue: Daemon SIGTERM while RUNNING: kill job group, set QUEUED, re-run once on next start.
    Agent->>Queue: sanctuary_daemon.py status (read results, then normal PR / closeout workflow)
